WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.250
Four decisions close this part, each
with one owner from the project plan.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:09.875
Identity engineering decides restriction,
unit by unit, before each unit exists.

3
00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:14.750
The CISO decides the persona set,
and the required affinity for PIV.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:20.062
And the ICAM governance body decides who
writes the binding after AD; that one

5
00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:25.375
can wait until issuance moves off AD CS,
which gives the open pilot time to report.

6
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:27.087
Watch the margins, too.

7
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:30.713
The tightest here is just two
working days, between the pilot's

8
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:34.624
shadow comparison and the program
assigning the pilot's policies.

9
00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:39.721
Part 3 takes Gates 7 to 9: proving one
mover across the tracks with no ticket,

10
00:00:39.721 --> 00:00:43.648
cutting over by attribute
query and retiring the OU tree,

11
00:00:43.648 --> 00:00:46.238
and then keeping the attributes true.

12
00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:47.060
Thank you.
